## erlang-ls project configuration for the Kazoo umbrella.
##
## Read as YAML -- erlang-ls bundles yamerl. (els_dap reads THIS SAME PATH with
## file:consult/1, expecting Erlang terms, so its `runtime' section is
## unreachable in practice and cannot be used to fix node identity; that lives in
## .vscode/launch.json + scripts/dev-node.sh instead. See issue #43.)
##
## apps_dirs point at SOURCE (core/*, applications/*), so navigation and
## diagnostics work the moment the tree is open -- before `make build-dev' has
## produced any _build output. erlang-ls degrades gracefully until then: an
## absent glob simply indexes nothing, so opening before the first build is
## fine, just less complete.
##
## deps_dirs points at _build/DEFAULT/lib, NOT _build/dev/lib -- deliberately.
## The dev release is dev_mode: every project app under _build/dev/lib is a real
## directory whose src/include/priv SYMLINK back to core/* + applications/*
## source (e.g. _build/dev/lib/crossbar/src -> ../../../../applications/crossbar/src).
## Globbing _build/dev/lib/* therefore re-indexes all 87 project apps a SECOND
## time -- once as apps (from apps_dirs) and once as deps -- which roughly doubles
## the project files walked at cold-index time and makes go-to-definition ambiguous
## between the source path and the _build/dev/lib/... copy. erlang-ls 0.0.46 has no
## `exclude_paths' key, so the fix is to point deps at _build/default/lib, which
## holds ONLY the 52 third-party deps (project apps are never built into default),
## each carrying its own real src/ for navigation. See issue #49.
##
## include_dirs feeds ONLY the compiler `{i,Dir}' options (els_compiler_diagnostics)
## and include-POI resolution -- NEVER indexing (els_indexing walks apps_paths +
## deps_paths + otp_paths only), so the entries below are additive and cannot
## re-introduce the double-index the deps_dirs note guards against.
##
## erlang-ls's compiler diagnostic is a plain `compile:file(F, [basic_validation,
## {i,Dir}...])' with NO code:lib_dir override. So an include_lib("app/include/x.hrl")
## resolves only when code:lib_dir(app) succeeds (it never does -- the project apps
## are not on erlang-ls's code path) OR when some {i,Dir} joins with the FULL
## "app/include/x.hrl" via epp's fallback -- i.e. Dir must be the PARENT of the apps
## (`core', `applications', `_build/default/lib'), NOT the leaf `app/include' dir.
## With only the leaf globs, EVERY cross-app include_lib fails, and each failed
## app-root header (crossbar.hrl, callflow.hrl, ...) orphans every record/type/macro
## it defines -- measured at 2207 errors across a 140-module sample, only 4 clean.
## Likewise a plain -include("app.hrl") from a module in a src/<subdir>/ needs the
## app's `src' root on the path. Adding the parents + src roots takes the same
## sample to 138/140 clean, 9 residual errors. See issue #49.
##
## The 9 residual errors are the irreducible parse_transform noise: erlang-ls
## applies NO parse_transform (not lager_transform, not kazoo_ast), so the handful
## of functions/specs those transforms generate read as undefined_function /
## spec_fun_undefined. Not fixable via macros:/include_dirs:; characterised, not
## silenced. (lager CALLS compile clean under basic_validation -- remote calls are
## never checked -- so lager is NOT a diagnostic-noise source despite the premise.)

apps_dirs:
  - "core/*"
  - "applications/*"

deps_dirs:
  - "_build/default/lib/*"

include_dirs:
  ## Parents -- resolve include_lib("app/include/x.hrl") via epp's {i,Dir} fallback.
  - "core"
  - "applications"
  - "_build/default/lib"
  ## src roots -- resolve plain -include("app.hrl") from src/<subdir>/ modules.
  - "core/*/src"
  - "applications/*/src"
  ## Leaf include/ dirs -- kept for plain -include of include/ headers and for
  ## include-POI navigation/autocomplete (els_include_paths).
  - "core/*/include"
  - "applications/*/include"
  - "_build/default/lib/*/include"
